HOW MANY VERSES? 
THREE GREEN BOTTLES STANDING ON THE WALL,
THREE GREEN BOTTLES;
IF ONE OF THOSE BOTTLES SHOULD HAPPEN TO FALL,
TWO GREEN BOTTLES STANDING ON THE WALL.

TWO GREEN BOTTLES STANDING ON THE WALL,
TWO GREEN BOTTLES;
IF ONE OF THOSE BOTTLES SHOULD HAPPEN TO FALL,
ONE GREEN BOTTLES STANDING ON THE WALL.

ONE GREEN BOTTLES STANDING ON THE WALL,
ONE GREEN BOTTLES;
IF ONE OF THOSE BOTTLES SHOULD HAPPEN TO FALL,
NO GREEN BOTTLES STANDING ON THE WALL.

HOW MANY VERSES? 